# You very likely do not need this file.
#
# The app derives the API host from Metro's own address — how your phone fetched
# the bundle in the first place — so emulator, simulator, physical device and web
# preview all work with no .env at all. See src/lib/api-url.ts.
#
# Set EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL only to OVERRIDE that: a staging API, a colleague's
# machine, or `expo start --tunnel` (which proxies Metro, not the API, and is
# deliberately not derived from).
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.staging.ejua.gh
#
# Inlined into the bundle at transform time, not read at runtime, so restart with
# `npx expo start -c` after changing it.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# Overrides just the port on the derived host, when the API is not on 3000.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT=3000

# NOTE: the other half of the configuration is NOT here and is not derivable.
# Image URLs are built from PUBLIC_API_URL in the REPO-ROOT .env, read by the API,
# not by Expo. Leave that at localhost and the app works while every picture
# renders blank, with nothing in either log. See ../../docs/design/object-storage.md.
